# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true, so a clone there checks every file out
# with CRLF while the index holds LF. The scrape runs from WSL and from Windows
# Python against that one worktree, and the two gits then disagree about whether
# anything is modified -- `git status` shows the whole tree dirty and a pull needs
# a stash. Pinning the working-tree ending settles it for every clone.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.zst binary
*.parquet binary
